<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">King of Anshan and Susa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anshan">King of Anshan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/susa">Susa</a> was a royal title of Elamite rulers, joining the names of the highland centre of Anshan and the lowland city of Susa. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sukkalmah-period">Sukkalmah period</a> it formed one tier of a tripartite governing hierarchy. According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elamite-confederation">Elamite Confederation</a> profile, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kidinuid-dynasty">Kidinuid dynasty</a> revived it around 1500 BCE as a unifying title asserting Elamite identity.</p></div>
